# xgboost:  3.3.0   (pinned in requirements.txt; enforced by src/analysis/common/_version_guard.py)
# R:        4.4.1 with ggplot2 4.0.3   (pinned in src/figures/R-requirements.txt; checked by make check-versions)
#
# produced: git clone <IGNITE> /tmp/verify && cd /tmp/verify && \
#             make tables PY=<pinned-python> RSCRIPT=<pinned-rscript> && \
#             make figures PY=<pinned-python> RSCRIPT=<pinned-rscript> && \
#             tools/write_baseline.sh <pinned-python> <pinned-rscript>
#
# IMPORTANT: the regenerated files hashed below are BUILD OUTPUTS. They are
# gitignored and are NOT in the commit -- you cannot 'git checkout' them. Rebuild
# with `make figures` (fast, no model fitting) and check with `make verify`.
#
# THE R VERSION ABOVE IS LOAD-BEARING. Rendering libraries change pixel output
# between releases and nothing guards R at render time, so a mismatched R stack
# produces figure mismatches that look like code regressions. Run
# `make check-versions` first; it checks both stacks.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES AND DOES NOT PROVE. Under the pinned R stack recorded above,
# the PNG hashes DO reproduce: 10 of 10 were byte-identical across two independent
# clones rendered through `make figures`. So a PNG mismatch on this machine is a real
# signal, usually a render that did not resolve .rlib and used a different ragg.
# What is not pinnable is the native rasterization stack -- ragg goes through
# freetype/libpng and the installed fonts (see src/figures/R-requirements.txt) -- so a DIFFERENT
# MACHINE can reproduce every NUMBER exactly and still fail these hashes.
#
# So `make verify-figures` reports rendered-PNG differences without failing, and the
# portable claim lives in `make verify-tables`: figure_data/ byte-identical to the
# commit after a rebuild. That is the check to trust for reproduction; this one is a
# same-machine regression check plus a tamper check on the artifacts no script can
# rebuild.
#
# 20 files: 20 regenerated outputs (the reproducibility-relevant subset),
# 0 frozen artifacts with no producing script, and 0 figure-provenance docs.
# Those three counts are COMPUTED, not typed.
#
# Was 38 before the two-stage restructure. What left, and why:
#   5  internal working documents, moved out of the repository entirely
#   1  causal_functional_genomics.png, dropped with its renderer as a strict subset
#      of the _with_thde figure
#   1  the pipeline schematic, DELETED -- stale depth=3 artwork, no producing script
